// The trailer, RC (#1178): Tools/trailer-cut.py Tools/trailer/trailer.json
// The RC is v8 with one change, the owner's on v8 (2026-11-20): the amphora in the net held 0.7 s longer (linelosshold= keeps the
// result page away), then 0.38 s of black in which the burn rings out over a break in the music, and the last shot on the beat
// with the music back at once. Two beats longer in all, so the action track's last chord still rings out on the end card.
// The owner on v7 (2026-11-20), and a review he passed on: the loss at the net must be a real swing under the line (Amphora: a
// handle shot off, the amphora swinging on the other); the last shot's break-up spread to its end, the last big piece falling into
// the cut to the logo, and no spare volley at an empty ceiling; the action after the big top at once, on the drums' first beat,
// with no black, no standing gun and no black balls in a night scene; a hard cut, not a muddy dissolve, out of the opening, and
// its first hit sooner; no dark band behind the titles, a soft shadow at the letters only; and the sound made over: no hits on the
// cuts, the game's own sound over the music, the music dipped under its big moments and far down under the laser.
// A HUD clip is never filmed with the benchmark's gun (its lens circles the gun): the shots it found are replayed by "hands" with the
// game's own camera, with the same turn= and walk= the finding run had. Camera paths count from a clip's window start, a quarter
// second before its "in".
